/-!
# Checkable rational distinction calculus

Finite observers, raw path proofs, independent derivation semantics,
proof-carrying least metric completion, simple-path completeness of
the graded indistinguishability fragment, weighted observation
accounting, the history event grammar, the U3 degeneracy result, and
exact connections to multiscale goals and structure-preserving repair.

This is a formalized fragment of the September 2026 distinction-calculus
papers, not a claim that their analytic, statistical, hive, or metacognitive
theories are completely formalized. Operational consumers import it in their
own layer rather than making generic cybernetics depend on a language runtime.
-/
